# Line endings are LF in the repo AND in the working tree, on every platform.
#
# Without this, `core.autocrlf=true` (the Windows/WSL default) rewrites text
# files to CRLF on checkout while storing them as LF. The stored content is
# fine, so `build` and the tests pass — but Prettier defaults to `endOfLine:
# "lf"`, so `npm run format:check` fails on all 43 source files the moment you
# switch branches. A gate that breaks on `git checkout` teaches people to ignore
# the gate.
#
# `eol=lf` (not just `text=auto`) is the part that matters: `text=auto`
# normalizes what gets *stored*, which was already correct here; `eol=lf` also
# pins what gets *checked out*.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries git must never touch. Sprites, artwork, the vendored fonts and the
# generated social images are all byte-exact — a line-ending "fix" applied to a
# woff2 or a png corrupts it.
*.png binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.woff2 binary
*.svg text eol=lf
